{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 11 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class e1542easy {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        int mod = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        solve(n, mod);\n    }\n\n    public static void solve(int n, int mod) {\n        List<long[]> inversions = new ArrayList<>();\n        inversions.add(new long[]{1});\n\n        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n            long[] prev = inversions.get(i - 1);\n            int len = i * (i + 1) / 2 + 1;\n            long[] curr = new long[len];\n\n            for (int j = 0; j < len; j++) {\n                long sum = 0;\n                for (int k = Math.min(j, i); k >= 0; k--) {\n                    if (j - k < prev.length) {\n                        sum = (sum + prev[j - k]) % mod;\n                    }\n                }\n                curr[j] = sum;\n            }\n            inversions.add(curr);\n        }\n\n        long[] ans = new long[n];\n        ans[0] = 0;\n\n        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n            long cur = (ans[i - 1] * (i + 1)) % mod;\n            long[] inv = inversions.get(i - 1);\n\n            for (int j = 0; j < inv.length; j++) {\n                for (int k = j + 2; k < inv.length; k++) {\n                    long diff = k - j;\n                    long m = Math.min(diff, i + 1);\n                    long coef = (m - 1) * (2L * i - (m - 2)) / 2;\n                    cur = (cur + ((inv[j] * inv[k]) % mod) * coef) % mod;\n                }\n            }\n            ans[i] = cur;\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(ans[n - 1]);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <sstream>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nvector<vector<long long>> solveInversions(int n, int mod) {\n    vector<vector<long long>> inversions;\n    inversions.push_back({1});\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n        vector<long long> prev = inversions[i - 1];\n        int len = i * (i + 1) / 2 + 1;\n        vector<long long> curr(len, 0);\n\n        for (int j = 0; j < len; j++) {\n            long long sum = 0;\n            for (int k = min(j, i); k >= 0; k--) {\n                if (j - k < (int)prev.size()) {\n                    sum = (sum + prev[j - k]) % mod;\n                }\n            }\n            curr[j] = sum;\n        }\n        inversions.push_back(curr);\n    }\n    return inversions;\n}\n\nvoid solve(int n, int mod) {\n    vector<vector<long long>> inversions = solveInversions(n, mod);\n\n    vector<long long> ans(n, 0);\n    ans[0] = 0;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n        long long cur = (ans[i - 1] * (i + 1)) % mod;\n        vector<long long> inv = inversions[i - 1];\n\n        for (int j = 0; j < (int)inv.size(); 